WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.970
Behind me is the
Royal London Homeopathic Hospital.

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:06.750
And I'm here because it's been an interesting
week for alternative medicine in Britain.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:11.290
This week, Noel Edmonds, television star,
and promoter of mid-90s fever dream Mr Blobby,

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:14.719
endorsed something called the EMP Pad.
It’s a yoga mat,

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:18.560
and its inventors claim that its very low
intensity electromagnetic fields

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.069
help cells in the body function.

00:00:20.069 --> 00:00:24.509
Now, I’m not going to go into loads of detail
about the evidence for the Pad.

00:00:24.509 --> 00:00:27.319
I’m very skeptical, but there are early
studies that say

00:00:27.319 --> 00:00:31.249
carefully applied, specific electromagnetic
fields may actually do some good.

00:00:31.249 --> 00:00:32.920
I know, I was surprised too.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.539
Okay, a yoga mat probably isn’t going to
work like that,

00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:38.989
but there are devices using EM fields that
are working well enough

00:00:38.989 --> 00:00:41.179
that insurers are starting to pay for them.

00:00:41.179 --> 00:00:45.160
I’ll also skip over the insulting reaction
that Noel Edmonds got from people on Twitter,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.129
particularly after he told someone
suffering from cancer

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:50.589
that it might be because of their
“negative attitude”.

00:00:50.589 --> 00:00:54.829
Instead, let’s look at the reaction of the
folks who make the EMP Pad.

00:00:54.829 --> 00:00:57.940
Because, okay, the skeptics won’t like them
whatever they do,

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.940
but there are plenty of
alternative medicine believers out there.

00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:03.589
Surely the company would welcome
a celebrity endorsement?

00:01:03.589 --> 00:01:10.090
No. At the top of their web site, in big letters,
they disavowed Noel Edmonds entirely.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.939
Nothing to do with us, they said.

00:01:11.939 --> 00:01:16.079
And the reason was: he’d claimed
they could help cure cancer.

00:01:16.079 --> 00:01:20.659
Now across Europe, advertising prescription
drugs and medical treatments to the public is banned.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:24.270
They can advertise to doctors, sure, but those
American drug adverts

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.710
with their list of side effects just don’t
happen here.

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:30.369
"Serious, sometimes fatal events
such as infections, lymphoma,

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:33.000
"or other types of cancer have happened.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.850
"Blood, liver and nervous system problems,
serious allergic reactions,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.850
"and new or worsening heart failure have occurred."

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:43.689
But in Britain, there are even stricter laws
about cancer treatments.

00:01:43.689 --> 00:01:46.869
You can’t get away with saying, "oh, it’s
not really a medical device",

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:49.009
or, "oh, it’s just some herbs".

00:01:49.009 --> 00:01:53.180
If you sell something to the public,
saying it can help or cure cancer,

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:54.509
you can be prosecuted.

00:01:54.509 --> 00:01:56.219
Even if it does cure cancer.

00:01:56.219 --> 00:02:00.299
The idea, back in 1939 when the law was passed,
still holds true today.

00:02:00.299 --> 00:02:05.820
Sell your cure to doctors. If you give them
an alternative medicine that works,

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.830
with evidence to convince them,
they’ll start prescribing it,

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:11.970
and you, the person who discovered it,
you’re probably in line for a Nobel Prize.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:16.580
And if they don’t start prescribing it:
well, it probably doesn’t cure cancer, does it?

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:19.360
If you’re selling your cure directly to
the public,

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:21.000
it's almost certainly not a cure.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.800
And it’s probably going to hurt people that
would otherwise go to the doctor.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.470
With this law, no-one has to prove
that your cure doesn’t work:

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:33.230
they just have to prove you’re selling it
without going through someone qualified.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.600
Noel Edmonds was in the clear when he said
“this cures cancer”.

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:37.830
I think he’s irresponsible,
but he can believe that,

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.040
and he’s not selling any yoga mats himself.

00:02:40.040 --> 00:02:45.250
"I then had my tumor destroyed by sound waves,

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:50.620
"proving yet again that energy
is at the heart of this issue."

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.340
But the folks who do sell them:

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.750
they needed to shut down that claim
right away,

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.710
or risk an investigation that
they would really want to avoid.

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:00.900
